# OS/2 diagnostics for silent renderer exits ("render process exited with
# code: 32527", no exceptq report).
#
# Apply from the repository root with:
#   git apply os2-patches/os2-diag-renderer-exit.patch
# Remove again with:
#   git apply -R os2-patches/os2-diag-renderer-exit.patch
#
# All added log lines are tagged [os2-diag] and marked TODO(os2).
#
# What it adds:
# - mojo InterfaceEndpointClient: logs messages dropped because the endpoint
#   had already disconnected, or rejected by the generated stub.
# - content RenderProcessHostImpl: logs Shutdown()/ShutdownForBadMessage()
#   (with stack) and every ProcessDied() with termination status, raw exit
#   code and whether the browser requested the shutdown.
# - content bad_message::ReceivedBadMessage: logs the reason.
# - content child_process_launcher_helper_os2.cc: logs (with stack) every
#   TerminateProcess() and ForceNormalProcessTerminationSync().
# - content renderer_main.cc (OS/2 only): SA_SIGINFO handler for SIGTERM,
#   SIGINT, SIGHUP, SIGQUIT and SIGABRT that logs signal, si_code, si_pid,
#   parent pid and thread, then executes INT 3 so exceptq writes a report
#   for the thread the signal arrived on (base::debug::StackTrace prints
#   nothing on OS/2), then re-raises the signal.
#
# Reading the results:
# - ProcessDied "shutdown_requested 0" + renderer "got signal 15 ... si_pid 0"
#   means the signal was generated inside the renderer (e.g. OS/2
#   XCPT_SIGNAL_KILLPROC delivered by kLIBC as SIGTERM). The exceptq report's
#   registration chain / stack dump shows the exception records involved.
# - A TerminateProcess / ForceNormalProcessTerminationSync / Shutdown line
#   with a stack means the browser terminated the renderer.
diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/content/browser/bad_message.cc b/src/3rdparty/chromium/content/browser/bad_message.cc
